[{:seon.task/name "an-interrupt-leaves-nothing-pending"
  :seon.task/plan "From jolt/wiki (8c50215; seen by session WIKI at its root's server, 2026-10-21; re-verify first, the code is unchanged since): after seon.root/interrupt! stopped (loop [] (recur)) with \"interrupted by root\", every later eval in that agent bounded by :timeout-ms 200 (and in its clone) answered \"interrupted by root\" in 0.3 ms instead of running to its bound. Cause as far as traced: seon.intr's pending atom is cleared only by seon.intr/clear-pending!, called from the nREPL interrupt op (seon.repl), which root's interrupt! (SIGUSR1) never sends; a set pending makes seon.intr/run start stopped. Not traced: why pending was set although an eval was running when SIGUSR1 came. Correct: an interrupt ends exactly the form it reached; with no form running it is recorded as a no-op, and nothing carries into the next form or into a clone. Deletes the pending carry-over."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.intr-test/an-interrupt-ends-only-the-form-it-reached seon.intr-test/a-clone-starts-with-nothing-pending}}]
